Upstream attribution
====================

McooBuildwithEase is a port of, and a derivative work of:

    Effortless Structure
    https://github.com/huskuraft/effortless
    Copyright (C) 2023-2025 huskuraft and contributors
    Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0

The following parts of that project are reused here:

  * The mod's business logic and data model, originally under the package
    `dev.huskuraft.effortless`. In this repository it has been renamed to
    `com.mcoo.buildwithease` and adapted to Minecraft 26.2.

  * The `common-api` interface layer of the Universal API project,
    https://github.com/huskuraft/universal-api, Copyright (C) 2024-2025
    huskuraft and contributors, also licensed under the GNU Lesser General
    Public License v3.0. It is vendored in this repository under the package
    `dev.huskuraft.universal.api` and remains under its original license and
    package name.

  * The `universal/vanilla` and `universal/fabric` platform adapters of the
    Universal API project, likewise vendored under `dev.huskuraft.universal`
    and rewritten against the Minecraft 26.2 API.

All upstream sources are redistributed here as source code, in full, with no
proprietary additions layered on top of them. The upstream package name
`dev.huskuraft.universal` is deliberately retained so that the provenance of
every vendored file stays unambiguous.


Changes made in this port
==========================

Minecraft 26.2 is not compatible with the 1.21.3 codebase upstream targets,
so the platform adapters were rewritten rather than patched:

  * Yarn mappings were replaced with Mojang official names; Minecraft 26.2
    ships unobfuscated and Yarn does not cover this version.
  * The rendering stack was migrated to the 26.2 pipeline: `RenderType`,
    `RenderStateShard`, `MultiBufferSource`, `ShaderInstance` and `GuiGraphics`
    no longer exist. The custom shader pipeline was dropped entirely, in line
    with the upstream project's own configuration.
  * The render layer abstraction was reworked. Upstream describes a render
    layer as a free combination of `RenderStateShard` components, but in 26.2
    the vanilla `RenderType` factory is package-private, so a third-party mod
    can only reuse the entries that already exist in `RenderTypes` — and those
    have their depth test, culling, blending and output target fixed. The
    upstream-shaped API could therefore only ever be an approximation, so it
    was replaced by an explicit `VanillaLayer` enumeration, and the shader
    registration mechanism (which had no implementation and could not work
    without `CoreShaders`, a class that no longer exists) was removed.
  * The custom radial build-mode menu was replaced by a grid of buttons.
  * Client entry points now use the Fabric API lifecycle events instead of
    mixin-based bootstrapping. One mixin remains, for client-side input
    interception, which has no official API equivalent.
  * Block entity serialization moved to the `TagValueInput` / `ValueOutput`
    interfaces, so clipboard capture and paste of block entities and container
    contents were reworked accordingly.

On top of the port, this project adds:

  * Structure export to `.litematic`, Sponge Schematic v3 (`.schem`) and Axiom
    blueprints, with an in-game file manager for choosing the destination.
  * A three-dimensional diagonal line build mode, defined by three successive
    clicks: start point, horizontal direction, and end height.
  * A three-dimensional clipboard preview rendered from real block models,
    with mouse-driven rotation, panning and zooming.

The upstream `common-api` files were modified in ten places:

  * `api/renderer/Renderer.java`
    Added `renderModelPreview`, and reworked scissor handling: Minecraft 26.2
    scissor is a stack, so a rectangle is pushed on entry and popped on exit
    one-to-one with the platform. The upstream implementation re-pushed the
    parent rectangle on pop, which made the platform's stack grow without
    bound and clipped everything after the first list entry.
    `renderBlockState` and `renderBlockEntity` no longer take a render layer:
    in 26.2 the block model picks its own pipeline, so a layer could not be
    honoured. `renderBlockState` now takes a vertex colour instead, which is
    how a block preview is tinted.
  * `api/gui/AbstractContainerWidget.java`
    Right-button drags are now forwarded, not just left-button drags, so that
    a widget can offer a distinct interaction per mouse button.
  * `api/gui/container/AbstractEntryList.java`
    The scrollbar is shown by default and its hit area matches its rendered
    width, so the content area lines up with the panel edge.
  * `api/gui/input/EditBox.java`
    The selection highlight goes through `renderTextHighlight`, which uses
    Minecraft 26.2's additive blend instead of an opaque fill.
  * `api/platform/Entrance.java`
    `findPlugin` returns an empty `Optional` when no plugin implementation is
    present, instead of throwing `NoSuchElementException` and taking the
    client down with it.
  * `api/renderer/RenderLayer.java`
    Render layers are now created from a `VanillaLayer` enumeration instead of
    from a free combination of render state components.
  * `api/renderer/RenderLayers.java`
    Reduced to the GUI layers actually in use. The `org.lwjgl.opengl.GL11`
    depth-compare constants are gone, so the API layer no longer depends on
    an OpenGL binding at all.
  * `api/renderer/VertexFormats.java`
    Points at the renamed render layer factory.
  * `api/events/impl/ClientEventRegistry.java`
    The shader registration event was removed, together with its interface.
  * `api/renderer/RenderStateFactory.java`
    Renamed to `RenderLayerFactory` and reduced to the render layer creation
    and the vertex format lookups.

Seven upstream files were removed, because the mechanism they described cannot
work on Minecraft 26.2 and no code path used them:

  * `api/renderer/Shader.java`
  * `api/renderer/LazyShader.java`
  * `api/renderer/Shaders.java`
  * `api/renderer/Uniform.java`
  * `api/renderer/programs/RenderState.java`
  * `api/renderer/programs/CompositeRenderState.java`
  * `api/events/render/RegisterShader.java`

The corresponding platform adapters were removed as well
(`vanilla/renderer/MinecraftShader.java`, `vanilla/renderer/MinecraftUniform.java`),
and `vanilla/renderer/MinecraftRenderStateFactory.java` was replaced by
`vanilla/renderer/MinecraftRenderLayerFactory.java`.

Five files are new and belong to this project alone:

  * `api/export/StructureExporter.java`
  * `api/renderer/PreviewBlock.java`
  * `api/renderer/PreviewCamera.java`
  * `api/renderer/VanillaLayer.java`
  * `api/renderer/RenderLayerFactory.java`


